sanctioned: this program uses Db.open + Db.withTransaction + Db.exec (SqlValue params) + Db.findWhere (backlog #61 — the SqlFragment-typed replacement for the removed Db.unsafeFindWhere) — the Go backend and ipê share the Sky stdlib surface but the Go reference emits Go+SQLite binaries while ipê emits Rust+sqlx; the SQLite in-memory behaviour and row-type representation differ enough that a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both backends. ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. `Db.findWhere` itself has no Go counterpart (it is an ipê-only addition), so this divergence is structural, not incidental. The typed Sql.column/Sql.int/Sql.gt combinator channel is exercised here to prove the WHERE clause can only be built through parameterized combinators — never a hand-built string.
